@startuml credentials-lifecycle
title Credential Lifecycle: Holder Relinquishment, Intrinsic Validity, and Registration Retention

|Base credential: canonical contract and intrinsic validity|
start
:Issue one canonical Credential contract\nwith 1..n subjects and 1..n holders;
:Before validFrom\nnot yet intrinsically valid;
:validFrom;
:Usable while intrinsically valid;
if (Holder relinquishes?) then (yes)
  :Credential_RemoveSelfAsHolder\ncontroller is exactly that holder;
  if (Current holder and another remains?) then (yes)
    :Invoke abstract\ncredential_removeSelfAsHolderImpl;
    :Consume old canonical contract;
    :Create exactly one replacement\nwithout that holder;
    :Preserve holder order, logical identity,\npayload, intrinsic validity, and profile fields;
    :Return Credential_RemoveSelfAsHolderResult\nwith replacementCredential : ContractId Credential;
    -> Usable while intrinsically valid;
  else (no)
    :Reject non-holder or final-holder removal;
    -> Usable while intrinsically valid;
  endif
else (no)
  if (Archive shared contract?) then (all holders)
    :Credential_ArchiveAsAllHolders\nevery holder authorizes jointly;
    :Terminate current canonical credential\nwithout replacement;
    stop
  else (no)
    :validUntil;
    :Intrinsically expired;
    stop
  endif
endif

note right
The base view is immutable in place. Relinquishment replaces the
contract but does not terminate the logical credential. Local wallet
removal, holder relinquishment, Daml archival, intrinsic expiry,
revocation or suspension, registration expiry, and deregistration
are distinct. A removed holder loses future stakeholder visibility
according to the concrete template, but previously observed ledger
history and data cannot be erased. Subjects, holders, and issuer
remain independent. Concrete replacement creation must satisfy the
implementing template's signatory and authorization rules.
end note

|Registry-enabled credential: registration continuity and retention|
start
:Register Credential;
:registeredAt;
:Retrievable according to visibility policy;
if (Holder relinquishment replaces credential?) then (yes)
  :Copy embedded registration metadata unchanged;
  :Atomically update contract-ID references\nor preserve stable logical identity;
  :Do not reset timestamps, expiry, fees, status,\nretention, audit, or history;
  -> Retrievable according to visibility policy;
else (no)
  :Registration reaches expiresAt;
endif
if (Retention extended by a\nregistry-defined operation?) then (yes)
  :Registration retained or replaced\naccording to registry policy;
  -> Retrievable according to visibility policy;
else (no)
  :Registration unavailable or removed;
  stop
endif

note right
The registration clock is independent of validFrom/validUntil.
Self-removal creates no registration gap and does not restart the
registration lifecycle. The generic result remains ContractId
Credential; stronger registered discovery is profile-specific.
Registration expiry, extension, removal, or deregistration does not
change intrinsic validity or constitute revocation.
end note

@enduml
